  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0024, and it is used to store information about agricultural and sideline products, employees, departments, purchase records, processing records, and sales records. The database has six tables: agricultural_and_sideline_products, employee, department, purchase_record, processing_record, and sales_record.\nThe agricultural_and_sideline_products table has four columns: product_id, product_name, origin, and primary key (product_id). The employee table has eight columns: employee_id, name, gender, telephone, position, department_id, joining_time, and primary key (employee_id). The department table has six columns: department_id, department_name, person_in_charge_id, department_responsibilities, total_number_of_people_in_the_department, and primary key (department_id). The purchase_record table has ten columns: product_id, purchase_time, purchase_quantity, purchase_person_id, purchase_price, shipper_name, shipping_address, shipping_time, shipper_phone, and primary key (product_id, person_in_charge_id, purchase_time). The processing_record table has six columns: product_id, processing_time, processing_quantity, person_in_charge_id, processing_cost, and primary key (product_id, person_in_charge_id, processing_time). The sales_record table has ten columns: product_id, sales_time, sales_quantity, salesperson_id, sales_price, sales_location, customer_name, customer_phone_number, customer_address, and primary key (product_id, sales_time, salesperson_id).\nThe foreign key constraints in the purchase_record and processing_record tables reference the employee table, and the foreign key constraints in the sales_record table reference the agricultural_and_sideline_products table. The foreign key constraints in the department table reference the employee table. The update and delete rules for the foreign key constraints are CASCADE and RESTRICT, respectively.\nIn summary, the rschema_0024 database schema stores information about agricultural and sideline products, employees, departments, purchase records, processing records, and sales records. The schema has six tables, each with its own set of columns and foreign key constraints. The primary keys and foreign key constraints ensure data integrity and referential integrity in the database.",
  "gold_question": "The management system of agricultural and sideline products processing enterprises aims to achieve the whole process management from acquisition, processing to sales, and record, track and analyze the operation of enterprises through a unified platform. The system not only includes product, employee and department management, but also covers the records of acquisition, processing, sales and other links. Agricultural and sideline products have information such as name, origin, acquisition price, processing cost, and sales price. Multiple departments of the enterprise collaborate, and each department has information such as department name, person in charge, contact information, total number of department personnel, and department responsibilities. Employee management includes employee number, name, gender, telephone number, position and entry time. Each time you purchase, you need to record the purchased products, quantity, purchaser information, consignor, purchase time, consignor telephone number, shipping address, shipping time, etc. When processing, record the processed products, quantity, processor, and processing time. When selling, record the sold products, quantity, salesperson, customer, sales time, and sales price.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0024.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0024\nCREATE TABLE `agricultural_and_sideline_products` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `origin` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `telephone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `joining_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `department_responsibilities` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_number_of_people_in_the_department` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `department_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`person_in_charge_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `purchase_record` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_person_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `shipper_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `shipping_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `shipping_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `shipper_phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`, `purchase_person_id`, `purchase_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`purchase_person_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `processing_record` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `processing_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `processing_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `processing_cost` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`, `person_in_charge_id`, `processing_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `processing_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`person_in_charge_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_record` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `sales_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `salesperson_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `customer_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `customer_phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `customer_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`, `sales_time`, `salesperson_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `agricultural_and_sideline_products` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
